- Write that body to a temporary markdown file and run:

  gh pr edit <%= pr_url %> --body-file <path-to-body-file>

- Update `pr.md` in the task folder so its frontmatter still includes
  `pr_url: <%= pr_url %>` and the final line is:

  <!-- COMPLETE pr_url=<%= pr_url %> is_draft=false -->

Constraints:

- DO NOT run `gh pr ready` — the hive runner owns that call and runs it only
  AFTER a credential-pattern secret-scan of the refreshed PR body passes.
  Running it from the agent would let a secret-bearing body go public for
  the window between your `gh pr edit` and the runner's revert.
- Do not push; hive verified the branch is clean and pushed before this prompt.
- Do not write any file other than `pr.md` and temporary files needed for
  `gh pr edit --body-file`. The runner writes `summary.md` after the secret
  scan and `gh pr ready` both succeed.
- Do not include `.env`, secrets, tokens, or unrelated file contents in the PR
  body.

## Completion — REQUIRED, and the last thing you do

The hive runner detects this stage as complete ONLY from the terminal marker in
`pr.md`, never from your process exiting or returning to an idle prompt. You are
NOT done until `pr.md` ends with this exact line — write it even if the PR body
was already correct, and do not stop, idle, or yield until it is present. No
other line may follow it.

